@page "/privacy"
@inject IAboutRepository AboutRepo

<PageTitle>Privacy · @_siteTitle</PageTitle>

<div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-4">
    <h1 class="fw-bold mb-0">Privacy</h1>
</div>

<div class="card-dark p-4">
    <p class="text-secondary small">Last updated: August 7, 2026</p>

    <h5 class="fw-semibold mb-2">1. Data Controller</h5>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        The controller responsible for data processing on this website is:
    </p>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_about?.LegalServiceProviderName))
        {
            @_about.LegalServiceProviderName<br />
        }
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_about?.LegalServiceProviderLocation))
        {
            @_about.LegalServiceProviderLocation<br />
        }
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_about?.LegalContact))
        {
            <a href="@($"mailto:{_about.LegalContact}")" class="text-decoration-none">@_about.LegalContact</a>
        }
    </p>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        The current controller details are also available in the <a href="/legal">Legal Notice</a>.
    </p>

    <h5 class="fw-semibold mb-2">2. Hosting and Infrastructure</h5>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        This service uses Microsoft Azure for application hosting, database services, telemetry,
        secure configuration, file storage, and AI-related processing. Cloudflare is used for DNS,
        transport security, caching, and protective edge services. Depending on the request and
        service configuration, these providers may process IP addresses, timestamps, requested URLs,
        browser and device information, diagnostic data, and security-related request metadata.
    </p>
    <ul class="text-secondary small">
        <li>Core application resources are configured for the Azure region Germany West Central.</li>
        <li>Microsoft Foundry components used by the coaching workflow are configured for Sweden Central.</li>
        <li>Application Insights records requests, dependencies, exceptions, and performance metrics.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        If you sign in, Microsoft Entra ID processes authentication identifiers and related login data.
        The website may set technically necessary ASP.NET Core authentication, antiforgery, OIDC nonce,
        and OIDC correlation cookies. Cloudflare may set a <code>cf_clearance</code> cookie after a security
        check. These cookies support authentication, request integrity, and platform security and are not
        used by Training Architect for advertising. Their lifetime depends on the applicable service,
        security configuration, and browser settings.
    </p>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        Microsoft and Cloudflare act as service providers under their applicable contractual terms.
        Processing may involve group companies or subprocessors outside the European Economic Area.
        Where required, such transfers must be protected by an adequacy decision, Standard Contractual
        Clauses, or another safeguard recognized under Chapter V GDPR.
    </p>

    <h5 class="fw-semibold mb-2">3. intervals.icu Integration</h5>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        When you connect an intervals.icu account, Training Architect uses the Athlete ID and API key
        you provide to retrieve training, activity, fitness, recovery, and wellness data on demand.
        This data is used to generate the assessment, recommendation, or training plan you request.
        A plan is sent back to intervals.icu only when you actively request an upload.
    </p>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        The credentials are transmitted over HTTPS to the application and its configured athlete-data
        and AI workflow services. The API key is not written to the Training Architect database.
        The Athlete ID is stored separately for access configuration and usage accounting as described below.
        intervals.icu processes data under its own privacy terms.
    </p>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        In your browser, the Athlete ID, API key, selected language, and athlete profile goal are stored
        in session storage by default and removed when the browser tab is closed. If you choose the
        remember option, they are stored in local storage until you disconnect and remove them or clear
        the browser storage. These browser values are not encrypted by the application and are accessible
        to scripts running for this website.
    </p>

    <h5 class="fw-semibold mb-2">4. Artificial Intelligence Services</h5>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        Training Architect uses Microsoft Foundry and Azure OpenAI to generate assessments,
        recommendations, and training plans. The data sent for an AI request may include your prompt,
        Athlete ID, intervals.icu API key, selected settings, and the training and wellness context
        required to produce the requested result.
    </p>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        Microsoft may temporarily retain request and response content for service operation and abuse
        monitoring in accordance with the applicable Azure service configuration and contractual terms.
        According to Microsoft's terms for Azure OpenAI, customer prompts, completions, and training data
        are not used to train foundation models made available to other customers.
    </p>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        Training and wellness information may reveal information about health and is therefore capable
        of constituting special-category data under Article 9 GDPR. Such data must be processed only with
        your explicit consent under Article 9(2)(a) GDPR. You provide this consent by selecting Connect
        after the consent notice shown in the intervals.icu connection form. You may withdraw consent at
        any time for future processing by disconnecting the account and contacting the controller.
    </p>

    <h5 class="fw-semibold mb-2">5. Stored Operational Data</h5>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        Training Architect does not write the retrieved intervals.icu training and wellness dataset to
        its Cosmos DB application database. The dataset and generated output are nevertheless processed
        transiently by the application, the athlete-data service, and the AI services involved in the request.
        The following operational data is stored:
    </p>
    <ul class="text-secondary small">
        <li>Athlete configuration: Athlete ID, access level, usage limits, lock status, and an optional account message.</li>
        <li>Usage counters: Athlete ID, request type and count, accounting period, and input, cached-input, and output token totals.</li>
        <li>Voluntary feedback: AI response ID, request type, positive or negative rating, and optional feedback tags.</li>
        <li>Telemetry: HTTP requests, dependency calls, exceptions, failures, performance metrics, and related technical metadata.</li>
    </ul>

    <h5 class="fw-semibold mb-2">6. Data Retention</h5>
    <ul class="text-secondary small">
        <li>Weekly usage counters are automatically deleted after 30 days.</li>
        <li>Monthly usage counters are automatically deleted after 365 days.</li>
        <li>Application Insights telemetry, including submitted feedback events, is retained for 30 days under the current infrastructure configuration.</li>
        <li>Athlete configuration is retained until it is no longer required for account access and usage limits or until a justified deletion request is fulfilled.</li>
        <li>Browser session storage is cleared when the tab is closed; remembered local storage remains until it is actively removed.</li>
        <li>Provider-side AI request and response retention is governed by the applicable Azure service configuration and contractual terms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h5 class="fw-semibold mb-2">7. Legal Basis for Processing</h5>
    <ul class="text-secondary small">
        <li>Article 6(1)(b) GDPR for processing necessary to provide a requested assessment, plan, upload, or account function.</li>
        <li>Article 6(1)(f) GDPR for secure and reliable operation, rate limiting, abuse prevention, diagnostics, and service improvement.</li>
        <li>Article 6(1)(a) and Article 9(2)(a) GDPR for consent-based processing of health-related training and wellness data.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        Providing intervals.icu credentials and training data is voluntary. Without this information,
        Training Architect cannot retrieve the dataset or generate personalized coaching results.
        The service does not make decisions that produce legal or similarly significant effects solely by automated means.
    </p>

    <h5 class="fw-semibold mb-2">8. Your Rights under GDPR</h5>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        Subject to the applicable legal conditions, you may request access to your personal data,
        correction of inaccurate data, erasure, restriction of processing, and data portability.
        You may object to processing based on Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Where processing is based on consent,
        you may withdraw that consent at any time with effect for the future. Withdrawal does not affect
        the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal.
    </p>
    <p class="text-secondary small">
        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the data protection supervisory authority
        responsible for the controller or with the authority at your habitual residence or place of work.
    </p>

    <h5 class="fw-semibold mb-2">9. Contact</h5>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">
        If you have questions about this privacy notice or the processing of personal data,
        please contact
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_about?.LegalContact))
        {
            <span>
                <a href="@($"mailto:{_about.LegalContact}")" class="text-decoration-none">@_about.LegalContact</a>.
            </span>
        }
        else
        {
            <span>the site operator using the contact details provided on the legal notice page.</span>
        }
    </p>
</div>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter(Name = "SiteTitle")]
    private string _siteTitle { get; set; } = "Brands Advisory";

    private AboutContent? _about;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        _about = await AboutRepo.GetOrCreateAsync();
    }
}